<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Italy</p><h1 class="st-title">Republic of Ossola</h1><p class="st-meta">1944 CE – 1944 CE · capital Domodossola</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The best-known partisan republic of wartime Italy, which governed the Alpine valleys around Domodossola for about forty days in 1944.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In September 1944 Italian partisan formations drove German and Fascist garrisons out of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/val-dossola">Val d'Ossola</a>, near the Swiss border, and entered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/domodossola">Domodossola</a> on 10 September. A provisional government junta was formed, presided over by the socialist <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ettore-tibaldi">Ettore Tibaldi</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The junta brought together members of the different anti-Fascist parties. In a few weeks it reorganised local government, schools, justice and food supply, and planned democratic reforms, while the Swiss border allowed contacts with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a>. Its experience of self-government later influenced debates on the Italian constitution.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In October 1944 German and Fascist troops of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/italian-social-republic">Italian Social Republic</a> launched an offensive and reoccupied the valley. Thousands of civilians and partisans fled into <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/swiss-confederation">Switzerland</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/republic-of-ossola.jpg" alt="Republic of Ossola" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Alessandro Vecchi · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Valle_Ossola.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1944 CE – 1944 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Domodossola</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Ettore Tibaldi</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Italian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Partisan Republic of Ossola</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1944&amp;focus=republic-of-ossola" aria-label="Republic of Ossola on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4877 555 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Republic of Ossola lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5197 811L5250 826"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5250 826h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5197 811h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5197 811h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1944&amp;focus=republic-of-ossola">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
